<h2>Key Achievements in 2025</h2>

<h3>Quality Excellence</h3>
<p>We achieved a 100% inspection pass rate in Q4 2025 — meaning every single part shipped in the final quarter of the year met or exceeded customer specifications. This was made possible by:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Upgraded in-line vision inspection systems on all major production lines</li>
  <li>Enhanced statistical process control (SPC) with real-time monitoring</li>
  <li>Additional quality training for all production staff</li>
  <li>Implementation of full traceability for every production batch</li>
</ul>

<h3>Market Expansion</h3>
<p>We entered four new export markets in 2025, bringing our total to 32 countries served:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>South America</strong> — expanded presence in Brazil and Argentina</li>
  <li><strong>Southeast Asia</strong> — new customers in Vietnam and Thailand</li>
  <li><strong>Eastern Europe</strong> — strengthened partnerships in Poland and Czech Republic</li>
  <li><strong>Middle East</strong> — new distribution agreements in UAE and Saudi Arabia</li>
</ul>

<h3>Product Range Growth</h3>
<p>We expanded our product catalog with five new nut subcategories, bringing our total product categories to 20:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Hex Nuts (DIN 933/934, M6-M36)</li>
  <li>Flange Nuts (DIN 6923, M6-M20)</li>
  <li>Nylon Insert Nuts (DIN 982/ISO 7040, M4-M24)</li>
  <li>Wheel Nuts (Grade 10.9/12.9, M18-M27)</li>
  <li>Slotted Nuts (DIN 935/ISO 7035, M6-M36)</li>
</ul>
<p>All new products are available with full OEM cross-reference numbers and are produced under ISO 9001; Our manufacturing facility is IATF 16949 certified.</p>

<h3>Manufacturing Investment</h3>
<p>Throughout 2025, we invested in upgrading our production capabilities:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Added 5 new CNC machining centers (bringing total to 80+)</li>
  <li>Upgraded 12 cold headers with servo-feed systems for improved precision</li>
  <li>Installed new induction heating systems for forging (30% more energy-efficient)</li>
  <li>Expanded our tooling department with 2 new EDM machines</li>
</ul>

<h2>Our Manufacturing Capabilities</h2>
<p>As of early 2026, Carelong operates:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Cold Headers:</strong> 20+ machines (M4-M24 range)</li>
  <li><strong>Forging Presses:</strong> 30+ machines (160-1000 ton, including new presses)</li>
  <li><strong>CNC Machining Centers:</strong> 80+ machines</li>
  <li><strong>Mechanical Presses:</strong> 33 units (160-2500 ton)</li>
  <li><strong>Inspection Rate:</strong> 100% (every part inspected before shipment)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Looking Ahead: 2026 Priorities</h2>
<p>As we build on the momentum of 2025, our priorities for 2026 include:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Further capacity expansion</strong> — two new 1000-ton forging presses already installed in Q1 2026</li>
  <li><strong>Digital transformation</strong> — implementing MES (Manufacturing Execution System) for real-time production tracking</li>
  <li><strong>Sustainability initiatives</strong> — reducing energy consumption per part by 15% through equipment upgrades</li>
  <li><strong>Product development</strong> — expanding our range of high-strength fasteners (Class 12.9 and above)</li>
  <li><strong>Customer service</strong> — reducing quotation response time to under 24 hours for all inquiries</li>
</ul>

<blockquote>To our customers, partners, and team members: thank you for making 2025 a record year. We look forward to serving you in 2026 with the same commitment to quality, reliability, and continuous improvement that has defined Carelong since 2005.</blockquote>

